==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|foreswear}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|forsweren|}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|forswerian||to swear falsely}}. More at {{prefix|for|swear|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|ɛə(r)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|forswears|forswearing|forswore|forsworn}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[renounce]] or [[deny]] [[something]], especially under [[oath]].
#*: {{quote-book|passage=Never to woo her more; but do '''forswear''' her.|author={{w|William Shakespeare}}|title={{w|The Taming of the Shrew}}|year=1592}}
#*: {{quote-book|passage=Like Innocence, and as serenely bold / As Truth, how loudly He '''forswears''' thy Gold!.|author={{w|John Dryden}}, translating {{w|Juvenal}}|title=Satires|year=1726|url=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=2L0DAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA192&dq=dryden+forswears+thy+gold&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwixluKCxrfRAhVDbbwKHa-eCkYQ6AEIQzAH#v=onepage&q=dryden%20forswears%20thy%20gold&f=false}}
#*: {{quote-book|passage=Either '''forswear''' fucking others or the affair is over.|author={{w|Philip Roth}}|title=Sabbath's Theater|year=1995|url=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=RqqYrLmrcbYC&pg=PA3&dq=forswear&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiQn-bmw7fRAhXCVbwKHVN3ADk4ChDoAQgvMAQ#v=onepage&q=forswear&f=false}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[commit]] [[perjury]].

